version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-14"
url: "https://github.com/thomas-k-waters/sagari"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - astronomy
  - supermassive black holes
  - Schwarzschild modeling
  - Bayesian optimization
  - Gaussian processes
abstract: >
  SAGARI replaces the nested parameter grids of orbit-superposition modeling campaigns with adaptive
  rounds: a scrambled Sobol initial design, refinement by feasibility-weighted Expected Improvement under a
  Gaussian-process surrogate with an explicit term for the model-to-model scatter of chi2, a stopping rule on
  smoothed parameter ranges, error-bar rounds that test the surrogate out of sample, and a posterior sampled
  on the final surrogate. It needs only the parameters and chi2 of each model.
